            $msg = @"
LIVE CAMERA PREVIEW - Requirements
═══════════════════════════════════════════
This mode renders OBS's Virtual Camera output directly into the preview
panel (via VLC), instead of polling OBS for screenshots every ~300 ms.
It's smoother and eliminates freezing while Settings or other dialogs
are open, but it needs a bit of setup:

1) DIRECTSHOW CAPTURE DRIVER
   This app bundles the driver needed to read a camera, so no extra
   install is normally required. If it's ever missing (e.g. a bundled
   file was removed), installing the full VLC Media Player once
   (videolan.org) also works - the app can borrow its driver instead.

2) WINDOWS 11 CAMERA SHARING MUST BE ENABLED
   Make sure Windows is fully updated, then allow more than one app to
   use the same camera at once:
     Settings -> Privacy & security -> Camera
     -> turn on "Let desktop apps access your camera"
   Without this, OBS and this app can't both read the Virtual Camera
   at the same time.

3) OBS ONLY PROVIDES ONE VIRTUAL CAMERA OUTPUT BY DEFAULT
   If you need this app to preview a DIFFERENT feed than what another
   program (e.g. Zoom) is already using from OBS's Virtual Camera,
   install an OBS plugin that adds extra virtual camera outputs (search
   "OBS Multiple Virtual Camera" plugin), enable it, then pick the
   matching device name in "Select Camera..." above.
"@
            Show-InfoPopup -Title "Live Camera Preview - Requirements" -Key "CameraPreviewInfo" -DefaultText $msg -Owner $dlg
        })
