    $btnWaitingRoomAutoAdmitInfo.Add_Click({
            $msg = @"
ZOOM AUTO-ADMIT — What it is

Watches the Zoom Waiting Room during a meeting and automatically
admits people you've already trusted, while anyone unrecognized still
waits for you to admit them yourself. This is experimental (relies on
UI Automation reading Zoom's own window), so treat it as a convenience,
not a security control.

──────────────────────────────────────────────
HOW TO ACTIVATE

1. Check "Enable Zoom Auto-Admit (experimental)" above and click Save.
2. An "Admit" button appears on the main screen next to Focus — it
   stays visible only while this setting is enabled.
3. Set "Auto-start (sec before meeting)" to how long before your
   scheduled meeting time the Waiting Room monitor should start
   itself automatically (uses the meeting schedule on the main screen).
4. You can also start it earlier by hand any time — just click the
   grey Admit button on the main screen. Handy if you want to get
   Zoom set up and ready before people start needing to be admitted.

HOW IT WORKS

  • Once a Zoom meeting is detected, the app scans the Waiting Room
    on a timer in the background (a single scan can take a few
    seconds up to about a minute depending on the machine).
  • Anyone on your trusted list is admitted automatically.
  • Anyone not on the list is left alone — admit them yourself in
    Zoom as usual.
  • When you manually admit (or remove) someone not on the list, the
    app notices and asks if you want to add them to the Auto-Admit
    list for next time.

READING THE ADMIT BUTTON

  • Grey   — Auto-Admit is off, no meeting, or it hasn't reached its
    auto-start time yet (click it to start monitoring manually).
  • Green/Blue pulse — armed and monitoring; Waiting Room is empty.
  • Orange + "Waiting: N" — someone unrecognized is waiting and
    needs a manual admit.

Click the Admit button any time to open the Zoom Auto-Admit List
manager, where you can toggle Auto/Manual per person or remove
entries.
"@
            Show-InfoPopup -Title "Zoom Auto-Admit — Setup & Info" -Key "ZoomAutoAdmit" -DefaultText $msg -Owner $dlg
        })
